# WifiScanner — WiFi Channel Analyzer
# Files: src/coordinator/Wifiscanner.h, Wifiscanner.cpp

## PURPOSE
Non-blocking WiFi channel scanner using promiscuous mode. Measures packet count and airtime.

## API
- startScan(channel, durationSec): Channel 1-13, duration 1-60s. Switches WiFi channel, enables promiscuous callback.
- loop(): Check completion, calculate results. Call from main loop.
- isScanning(): true during active scan
- hasResult(): true when result ready (one-shot, cleared on getResult)
- getResult(): returns ScanResult, clears ready flag
- restoreChannel(channel): abort scan and restore original WiFi channel

## SCAN RESULT
- channel: scanned channel
- packets: total packets detected
- busy_ms: estimated airtime = (packets * 200µs) + (totalBytes / 2)
- total_ms: scan duration

## INTERNALS
- promiscCallback (IRAM): increments volatile packetCount + totalBytes per packet
- Airtime model: 200µs overhead/packet + 0.5µs/byte (averaged across 802.11 rates)
- busy_ms clamped to not exceed total_ms
